From b497cb5ed3f949753d8fdde6ad4aefd27512f9be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:50:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 102/105] dt-bindings: ufs: qcom,sc7180-ufshc: Add SM8475 UFS
 controller

The SM8475 UFS host controller is the SM8450 controller, but its core,
UniPro and ICE clocks run at up to 850 MHz. Above 300 MHz the controller
needs an SoC-specific turbo programming sequence, so the driver must be
able to tell the two SoCs apart.

Document "qcom,sm8475-ufshc" with "qcom,sm8450-ufshc" as fallback.

Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>

Import-Patch: pkgs/linux-kernel/sm8475/asphalt/patches/local/0033-sm8475-ufs-dt-bindings.patch
Import-SHA256: e3a108227e7643c3bd92893b4ed6d5d0f52fef5988815915ce335a75210f24ab
Import-Provenance: mail headers
(cherry picked from commit 4b4a98e20840061480c7c56f77daf46073ffa188)
